course: dictionary
lesson: 15952
title: Unsuited: not the right fit
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Unsuited means not right or not suitable for a person, job, place or purpose. You can work out its meaning from the words around it. «Ben's thin trainers were unsuited to the snowy mountain path.» Thin trainers do not keep you warm in snow, so unsuited must mean not right for snow.
explain: Look for the clue that tells you what something is not right for. «The little tent was unsuited for six people.» A tent that is too small for six people is not a good fit for them, so unsuited means not suitable. Test it: put "not suitable" in place of unsuited and check the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Unsuited is often followed by "to" or "for": unsuited to, unsuited for. You may also meet ill-suited, which means the same thing. «Her tiny flat was ill-suited to a big dog.» Both words mean that something does not fit well.
fact: Unsuited means not right or not suitable for a person, job, place or purpose.
fact: «Unsuited» is often followed by «to» or «for», as in «unsuited to hiking».
fact: «Ill-suited» is another phrase with the same meaning as unsuited.
fact: A good check is to swap in "not suitable" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «Thin sandals are unsuited to a snowy mountain.» What does unsuited mean here? | Warm and cosy | Very cheap | Brand new | *Not right or not suitable for snow
exercise: «The little tent was unsuited for six people.» What is the tent unsuited for? | Sleeping six people | Being bright and colourful | Cooking dinner | *Sleeping six people comfortably: it is too small
Oops
exercise: Mum says her heavy winter coat is unsuited to a hot beach. What does unsuited mean? | Cheap to buy | Easy to wash | *Not suitable for a hot beach | Covered in gold
test: «The old bridge was unsuited to heavy lorries.» What does unsuited mean? | Painted bright red | Strong enough for lorries | *Not suitable for heavy lorries | Very new
test: Kai says he is ill-suited to the job. What does that mean? | He is perfect for the job | He is leaving the job | He is very tired | *He is not the right person for the job
exam: Which phrase best explains unsuited? | *Not right or not suitable for a person, job, place or purpose | Very large and heavy | Quick and loud | Very happy and excited
